{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of J4 setup Source V11 for adoption, for request 453fa6ea. Verdict: APPROVED, adopting this operator source for the one J4 setup run, and releasing nothing.\n\nEvidence body SHA-256: 4997254d95a969fc64becd11203ed7216b37c0d3c3fdedce4bdd3600a4730717\nOperator Source SHA-256: d18e120eaa0309bac4d3a6fc6dfc5c055fb97e41ed231e6376b21c22fbc7ee48\n\nThis adopts the operator only. It releases no admission, read or setup, and it claims no J4 or S1 result. If either file above changes, this review no longer applies. The Source is `source-index.json` f814ec23, with all 83 index rows verified.\n\nI read the diff from V10 of `operator.mjs` and `setup-native.mjs`, and `safety.mjs` and `setup.mjs` don't change. I checked the qualifier and rehearsal captures, and I read `verifyActualReview`. I ran no second independent read on this small delta. The independent read of V9 and V10 covers the routes and the rehearsal's sources.\n\n## My items\n\n- Item 1: ruling 8f2f7140 settles it. `operation` in `setup-native.mjs` follows it, and the plan lists which operations fall on which side.\n- Item 2: `setupTokens` and `forkAttempts` list every setup token and fork attempt per hold with its state and no body, and `completeClassification` gives `setup-complete-leftovers-open` when one stays, or when a record is missing. The `retries` capture shows token 1 still `minting`, with the fork's first attempt open, and that word.\n- Item 3: `poll` records reads, moved reads, elapsed milliseconds and how it ended, per site. `msAfterOpening` adds native time per outcome.\n- Item 4: `settled` reads again on a moved head at the four sites, within a small bound, and the comparison after each read still stops on a real difference. `moved-at-settle` shows it.\n\n## The captures\n\n- Qualifier: receipt a7b0886d and stdout 48f3d1f7 carry the stated digests. It exited 0 with `setup-112-source-filesystem-qualified`, 52 cases, zero network and private path attempts, and the source unchanged.\n- Rehearsal: receipt 605412e9 names this source index and shows the operator at d18e120e in all ten scenarios, each matching its expected end, with the requests you list. `clean` ran with no leftover, and the fork poll shows moved reads even locally.\n- Evidence copy: its `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 2f052533, with 4,430 files, none writable.\n- Both worktrees are clean at their pins, 112eff12 and 5dc9765f, and live health reports da13242c.\n\n## Your points\n\na. Accepted. The extra halts are honest, and each has a fixed word. For the planner: a hanging fork halts with its third attempt unrun.\n\nb. Accepted. One window covers the three operations for a hold, and the plan says so.\n\nc. Accepted, with the words kept honest. `fork-refused` reads `setup-complete` with the refused row public. A refusal means native records nothing left behind, not that the provider holds no fork. The J4 report must say that no read proves it.\n\nd. You're right, and my V10 report was wrong. Token 1 stays `minting` and token 2 is `ended`, because a refusal ends its token.\n\ne. Accepted.\n\nf. Accepted. 176.70 s of 180 s and 185 of 192 requests are arithmetic, not a run. `pollTimes` will replace that arithmetic.\n\ng. Accepted. The J4 report must say that the record ends at the last read and native keeps running after a halt.\n\nh. It has no bearing on this capture, since the released run didn't hit it. A rerun on a shared machine could.\n\n## Conditions for release\n\nThese bind Root and the planner, and this review doesn't discharge them:\n\n1. Read this act with `git show`, and read `statement.retired` with `gs inspect`, for this report and for 71fddd54. Stop if either is retired. Stale alone doesn't stop it.\n2. Worker da13242c must still be deployed. Main has moved past 112eff12, and a deployment before setup voids this source. Main's later landings are fine as long as no Worker changes.\n3. The stops in `PLAN.md` apply in order, and the admission writer and the setup command each need their own release. `verifyPacket`, collector main and the finalizer at a real path have never run, so a refusal there is expected to be possible and costs nothing in the room.\n4. Inspect `stderr.log` before sealing, and keep the private run out of evidence.\n5. No retry. One try per room, under 8f2f7140, and a halt past the first original costs this room and vault.\n\n## What the J4 report must state\n\n- Only R01 to R07 have proof under da13242c. Most writes are first-time, and R28 to R30 have no proof under any Worker. The real provider has never run this path.\n- The rehearsal uses policy generation 2 where the real room has 3, and nobody traced the room's real history through every row.\n- The Membership window, key presence and mode only for the planner's item 10, the slow-Worker case at head, and unmeasured write latency.\n- Every leftover by name, for the planner to handle.\n- Register stays unobserved. The two S1 summary 403s stay unexplained.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe operator stays one reviewed file, and the additions are records and bounded rereads. The design carries V14's weight, and that's why it took this many rounds. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nNo authority is widened, no path resends an original, and public output holds fixed words, public names and counts, with no body or credential. A leftover token is now visible and doesn't read as clean. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nReplacing `movedHeadReads` with one poll record and adding one classification word is the smallest honest form. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- This adopts the operator at the two digests above. The real test is the live run, and this review proves nothing about it.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8b0e3afad9bcf78504767c1f83f8172b39ca9452 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1